---
import GuideLayout from "../../layouts/GuideLayout.astro";
import Surface from "../../components/ui/Surface.astro";
import Button from "../../components/ui/Button.astro";
import { guides } from "../../data/guides";
import { siteLinks } from "../../data/site";

const guide = guides.find(
  (entry) => entry.slug === "offline-dictation-on-mac",
)!;
---

<GuideLayout
  guide={guide}
  intro="For offline speech-to-text, install a local speech model and use local refinement or turn refinement off. These choices keep dictation processing on your Mac after the required models are installed."
>
  <Surface class="guide-section">
    <h2 id="requirements">What you need</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>An Apple silicon Mac running macOS 15 or later.</li>
      <li>
        Airdraft installed, with Microphone and Accessibility permissions.
      </li>
      <li>An internet connection for the initial model downloads.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Apple SpeechAnalyzer and Apple Intelligence need macOS 26 or later. Apple
      Intelligence also needs to be available on your Mac. Other local speech
      models do not require Apple Intelligence.
    </p>
    <p>
      Start with the <a href={siteLinks.build}>source build instructions</a>.
      The <a href="/pricing/">pricing page</a> lists current official-app
      availability.
    </p>
  </Surface>

  <Surface class="guide-section">
    <h2 id="setup">Set up your first local dictation</h2>
    <ol class="guide-steps">
      <li>
        <h3>Allow recording and text insertion</h3>
        <p>
          Grant Microphone when prompted. Enable Airdraft in System Settings →
          Privacy &amp; Security → Accessibility so it can insert text.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Download and select a local speech model</h3>
        <p>
          Open Models and choose a local model that supports your language.
          Airdraft downloads models only when you request them. An installed
          model loads automatically when you start dictating.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Choose local cleanup, or skip it</h3>
        <p>
          In Models → Refinement, choose Apple Intelligence on a supported
          system, or connect LM Studio or Ollama running locally on this Mac.
          For speech-to-text without AI cleanup, turn off Refine transcript for
          your active profile in Profiles.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Check the active profile</h3>
        <p>
          A profile can have its own speech model. In Profiles → Speech model,
          choose a local model or Use App Default to follow Models. A cloud
          speech binding would still send audio to that provider.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Hold, speak, release</h3>
        <p>
          Put your cursor in a text field. Hold Control + Option, speak, then
          release. Airdraft transcribes and refines after recording stops, then
          inserts the result. You can change the shortcut in Configuration.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </Surface>

  <Surface class="guide-section">
    <h2 id="languages">Which model should I choose?</h2>
    <p>
      Language support belongs to the model. Parakeet TDT v3 supports English
      and 24 other European languages, but not Mandarin or Cantonese. For mixed
      Chinese and English, Airdraft's setup instructions recommend Qwen3-ASR
      1.7B. Choose your output script under Models → Speech options → Chinese
      script.
    </p>
    <p>
      Local processing uses your Mac's memory and compute. Model loading and
      transcription time vary with the model and hardware; the website's
      interactive sample is an illustration, not a speed test.
    </p>
  </Surface>

  <Surface class="guide-section">
    <h2 id="offline-scope">What does offline cover?</h2>
    <p>
      Local speech and local refinement do not need a cloud model to process
      your dictation. Initial downloads, app updates and official-app licensing
      are separate network activities. A custom endpoint on another computer is
      not processing on this Mac.
    </p>
    <p>
      Read{" "}
      <a href="/guides/local-vs-cloud-dictation/">
        what each model choice sends
      </a>{" "}
      before mixing local and cloud engines.
    </p>
    <div class="guide-actions">
      <Button href="/support/" icon="right">
        Troubleshoot Setup
      </Button>
      <Button href={siteLinks.build} variant="quiet" icon="external">
        Source Build Instructions
      </Button>
    </div>
  </Surface>
</GuideLayout>
